WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:14.293
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:14.563 --> 01:16.271
Come out!

3
01:27.438 --> 01:32.438
The Phii Pong comes out to hunt at night.

4
01:32.980 --> 01:35.355
Once it catches its prey,

5
01:35.438 --> 01:37.271
it kills,

6
01:37.355 --> 01:39.021
rips open the stomach,

7
01:39.105 --> 01:40.521
pulls out the entrails,

8
01:40.605 --> 01:42.438
and devours them.

9
01:42.521 --> 01:47.396
DELUSION

10
01:52.021 --> 01:53.396
-Yuck. -Yuck.

11
01:54.896 --> 01:56.730
If anyone happens to see its face,

12
01:56.813 --> 01:58.438
the Phii Pong

13
01:58.521 --> 02:00.230
will kill that person right away.

14
02:00.313 --> 02:02.188
Otherwise, it will die instead.

15
02:02.271 --> 02:03.980
After the kill,

16
02:04.063 --> 02:06.188
it will eat that person's guts too.

17
02:07.480 --> 02:10.771
Won't it get diarrhea in the morning?

18
02:11.771 --> 02:13.438
No. It's a ghost.

19
02:13.521 --> 02:14.896
What?

20
02:14.980 --> 02:17.605
But you said it turns human during the day.

21
02:17.688 --> 02:22.188
They say your mother's village is full of Phii Pong.

22
02:22.271 --> 02:26.313
Watch out when she takes you there. You might get eaten.

23
02:34.230 --> 02:37.355
-Wow. -Food's here.

24
02:37.438 --> 02:38.480
Wan.

25
02:38.980 --> 02:40.730
-Yes? -The food is very delicious.

26
02:40.813 --> 02:44.980
Did you order it from Bangkok? Yote told me you found the caterer.

27
02:45.063 --> 02:46.438
I'd love to get their number.

28
02:46.521 --> 02:49.271
Sure. I'll give it to you.

29
02:49.355 --> 02:53.105
I'm so jealous of Sunee. She's lucky to have you as her daughter-in-law.

30
02:54.855 --> 02:57.188
Wan, how have you been?

31
02:58.063 --> 02:59.688
I'm doing well.

32
03:00.438 --> 03:03.480
A capable person like you should've been promoted to principal by now.

33
03:04.105 --> 03:05.813
You've been vice principal far too long.

34
03:15.521 --> 03:16.730
Please excuse me.

35
03:16.813 --> 03:17.771
Sure.

36
03:22.021 --> 03:23.396
Don't just sit there chatting.

37
03:23.480 --> 03:24.771
Raise your glasses!

38
03:25.980 --> 03:27.188
Come on.

39
03:27.271 --> 03:28.146
Cheers.

40
03:28.230 --> 03:30.105
Cheers, everyone.

41
03:30.188 --> 03:31.688
-Congratulations. -Congratulations.

42
03:31.771 --> 03:33.646
Mrs. Wan, you've got a delivery.

43
03:33.730 --> 03:34.646
I'll take care of it.

44
03:35.230 --> 03:36.938
The customer has ordered some more.

45
03:40.605 --> 03:43.271
CASH SALE FIVE CASES OF CHAMPAGNE, 39,000 BAHT

46
03:48.105 --> 03:50.105
-Bring it inside. -Okay.

47
03:50.188 --> 03:54.938
50TH ANNIVERSARY APPRECIATION BANQUET KANG CHAI LIMITED PARTNERSHIP

48
03:55.021 --> 03:58.813
SPONSORED BY LOEI FORWARD GROUP

49
03:58.896 --> 04:00.771
-Cheers. -Thank you for today.

50
04:00.855 --> 04:02.105
-Thank you. -Congratulations.

51
04:02.188 --> 04:03.605
-Thank you. -Congratulations.

52
04:32.355 --> 04:34.855
You can head back first.

53
04:37.605 --> 04:39.730
I'll have Aim sleep at my mom's.

54
04:42.313 --> 04:43.730
Can you drive?

55
04:44.605 --> 04:45.480
Of course.

56
04:47.271 --> 04:49.688
Just drink all you want.

57
04:49.771 --> 04:51.521
I can take him home.

58
04:52.730 --> 04:55.855
I already told Mom Aim's staying at her place.

59
05:06.646 --> 05:08.355
Just wire it back to me when you have time.

60
05:14.646 --> 05:16.480
You paid it with my family's money anyway.

61
05:17.605 --> 05:20.355
Consider this your contribution to the party, then.

62
05:22.980 --> 05:23.980
Learn to invest.

63
05:25.980 --> 05:28.146
You spent so much money on your family.

64
05:28.230 --> 05:29.438
This is nothing.

65
05:29.938 --> 05:30.980
Here.

66
05:48.146 --> 05:50.105
Did your grandparents get diarrhea?

67
05:50.188 --> 05:53.021
My grandparents are not Phii Pong.

68
05:53.938 --> 05:56.230
Stay there long enough, and you'll find out.

69
05:56.855 --> 06:00.813
My mom said your parents are separating.

70
06:01.521 --> 06:04.855
You'll have to go live with your grandpa. You won't be living here.

71
06:04.938 --> 06:06.521
Boo!

72
06:06.605 --> 06:08.980
What are you guys playing here?

73
06:09.063 --> 06:10.730
What are you playing here?

74
06:14.355 --> 06:16.896
The lychees are ready. Come on, before the ice melts.

75
06:16.980 --> 06:19.355
-Okay. -Come on. Let's go.

76
06:19.438 --> 06:20.896
Let's eat some lychees.

77
06:21.855 --> 06:24.230
MOM

78
06:33.146 --> 06:34.271
What's up, Mom?

79
06:34.355 --> 06:36.813
Wan, come check on your dad.

80
06:36.896 --> 06:39.855
I don't know what's gotten into him. He's pacing around with a knife.

81
06:40.396 --> 06:41.771
What is it this time?

82
06:46.521 --> 06:47.605
Come out!

83
06:55.563 --> 06:57.480
I said come out!

84
06:58.230 --> 07:00.355
Mom.

85
07:00.438 --> 07:02.230
-Mom. -Hey!

86
07:04.980 --> 07:06.021
Mom.

87
07:06.105 --> 07:07.105
Mom.

88
07:07.646 --> 07:08.605
Mom!

89
07:12.355 --> 07:18.646
WAN

90
07:18.730 --> 07:21.730
FOUR MISSED CALLS

91
07:37.146 --> 07:39.480
50TH ANNIVERSARY APPRECIATION BANQUET

92
07:52.896 --> 07:55.355
-Cheers. -Cheers.

93
07:59.855 --> 08:01.146
Aim.

94
08:01.230 --> 08:02.438
Let's go, Son.

95
08:02.521 --> 08:04.063
-I have to go, Jae Ki. -You're leaving?

96
08:04.146 --> 08:05.188
Goodbye.

97
08:05.938 --> 08:07.605
Goodbye, Auntie Wan.

98
08:30.813 --> 08:31.980
What is it, Wan?

99
08:32.480 --> 08:34.188
Something's off with Dad. I'm heading home.

100
08:34.271 --> 08:35.896
Huh? Dad?

101
08:35.980 --> 08:37.771
Doctor, the patient's ready now.

102
08:38.313 --> 08:40.355
Wan, I'm tied up with a patient now.

103
08:40.438 --> 08:42.896
Please check on Dad for me.

104
08:51.896 --> 08:54.188
Just sleep. We're not there yet.

105
08:57.605 --> 09:02.146
You can leave me home alone. I'm all grown up.

106
09:05.855 --> 09:06.980
Why?

107
09:07.480 --> 09:09.980
Can't you keep me company?

108
09:11.605 --> 09:14.105
It's so boring at Grandpa's.

109
09:14.605 --> 09:15.980
There's nothing to do there.

110
09:16.521 --> 09:18.396
It's so hot without air conditioning.

111
09:19.605 --> 09:21.313
How is it hot?

112
09:21.396 --> 09:22.938
It's not hot at all.

113
09:23.021 --> 09:26.105
It's nice and cool. There are trees everywhere.

114
09:27.105 --> 09:29.605
Trees aren't the same as air conditioning.

115
09:40.563 --> 09:44.896
NASAO VILLAGE NASAO, CHIANG KHAN, LOEI

116
09:44.980 --> 09:48.896
CHIANG KHAN POLICE STATIONO

117
09:48.980 --> 09:50.605
POLICE MAJOR SASIDIT DESAYAKUL

118
09:52.896 --> 09:56.605
INVESTIGATION DIVISION CHIANG KHAN POLICE STATION

119
09:56.688 --> 09:58.938
CAPT. BIRD: I HEARD YOU MOVED TO CHIANG KHAN, PETE

120
09:59.021 --> 10:00.646
I'M HERE WITH MY BOSS. LET'S MEET UP.

121
10:02.771 --> 10:06.313
Are you going to the village headman's grandson's ordination this Sunday?

122
10:07.021 --> 10:09.230
I'll give him a donation. I can't be bothered to go.

123
10:10.688 --> 10:11.771
What?

124
10:12.438 --> 10:14.688
There will be beer and whiskey at the ceremony.

125
10:14.771 --> 10:16.563
Think of it as a chance to relax.

126
10:19.521 --> 10:21.646
Want a cigarette? It'll keep you awake.

127
10:21.730 --> 10:22.605
Let's go.

128
10:24.230 --> 10:25.605
You're going to the ordination?

129
10:25.688 --> 10:27.521
Please give them my donation.

130
10:28.980 --> 10:29.813
Here.

131
10:30.396 --> 10:31.438
Take it.

132
10:31.521 --> 10:32.355
Okay.

133
10:34.063 --> 10:36.563
-Let's go. -How's the missing person case going?

134
10:37.688 --> 10:38.521
Huh?

135
10:40.188 --> 10:42.938
His grandmother filed a report, Sergeant.

136
10:43.438 --> 10:46.313
The kid must have returned home by now.

137
10:46.938 --> 10:49.896
That's just how kids are around here, Inspector.

138
10:49.980 --> 10:53.105
They're either out with friends or passed out drunk somewhere.

139
10:53.188 --> 10:54.730
Were you like that too?

140
10:54.813 --> 10:55.855
What?

141
10:56.980 --> 10:58.605
The kid is 16, right?

142
10:58.688 --> 10:59.855
Yes, have a look.

143
11:01.605 --> 11:04.438
His name is Mued. He's Grannie Paew's grandson.

144
11:05.563 --> 11:07.771
He's been missing for over 24 hours.

145
11:07.855 --> 11:09.855
You know where they live, Sergeant?

146
11:10.980 --> 11:11.980
Yes.

147
11:12.063 --> 11:13.188
Good.

148
11:13.688 --> 11:16.355
Take me there. I'll wait for you outside the station.

149
11:18.646 --> 11:20.355
-Damn it. -Here we go.

150
11:20.438 --> 11:22.605
I didn't even get to smoke or drink.

151
11:23.605 --> 11:25.271
-Let's go. -Hurry up.

152
11:41.146 --> 11:42.855
Who's that? What are you doing here?

153
11:42.938 --> 11:44.438
Grandpa-Rong. It's Grandpa-Rong!

154
11:48.313 --> 11:49.313
Grannie Paew.

155
11:50.521 --> 11:52.813
Grannie Paew.

156
11:52.896 --> 11:54.063
The police are here.

157
12:00.063 --> 12:03.021
Just stay there. Don't come out. You might fall.

158
12:03.105 --> 12:04.771
Have you found him?

159
12:04.855 --> 12:06.146
No, not yet.

160
12:06.230 --> 12:08.521
This officer is here to help look for him.

161
12:15.521 --> 12:20.605
MUED

162
12:21.188 --> 12:22.771
It's a ghost-warding effigy.

163
12:23.938 --> 12:26.480
Every household with a man puts one outside.

164
12:26.563 --> 12:28.605
It's to keep ghosts from taking him away.

165
12:29.146 --> 12:30.855
It's what people do around here.

166
12:44.813 --> 12:45.896
Grannie.

167
12:45.980 --> 12:48.813
Where does your grandson sleep? Can you show me?

168
13:03.980 --> 13:05.813
Come in, Officer.

169
13:17.230 --> 13:19.230
Where does your grandson keep his belongings?

170
13:46.688 --> 13:48.563
Is he no longer in school?

171
13:49.855 --> 13:52.688
He dropped out over a year ago.

172
13:56.480 --> 13:58.896
Has anything valuable gone missing?

173
13:58.980 --> 14:00.563
No.

174
14:00.646 --> 14:03.313
Before he left, he even left me some money.

175
14:10.230 --> 14:12.688
Where did he get the money from?

176
14:14.063 --> 14:15.521
What did you find, Sergeant?

177
14:15.605 --> 14:17.480
What are these tracks?

178
14:19.396 --> 14:21.980
-Inspector, I found tire tracks… -Check the kid's motorcycle.

179
14:22.063 --> 14:24.063
Multiple previous owners. Plate can't be traced.

180
14:24.146 --> 14:25.813
If you find anything,

181
14:25.896 --> 14:28.480
notify our patrol officers and neighboring stations.

182
14:28.980 --> 14:29.813
Yes, sir.

183
14:32.938 --> 14:37.771
Do kids around here get together to race motorcycles or drink somewhere?

184
14:37.855 --> 14:38.730
No, sir.

185
14:39.896 --> 14:42.646
Most of them drink in town.

186
14:42.730 --> 14:46.021
-Or they drink out in the fields. -What about the forest?

187
14:47.771 --> 14:51.313
Nobody dares wander into the forest, Officer.

188
14:51.396 --> 14:55.063
It's infested with ghosts. Everyone around here knows that.

189
14:55.146 --> 14:57.980
If you wander in, you'll end up getting eaten.

190
14:58.563 --> 14:59.396
What kind of ghosts?

191
14:59.480 --> 15:00.938
Phii Pongs.

192
15:01.021 --> 15:04.480
They hunt frogs and toads in the forest.

193
15:05.188 --> 15:07.688
If you're unlucky enough to run into one, it'll eat your guts.

194
15:07.771 --> 15:09.730
How about this?

195
15:09.813 --> 15:13.938
Tomorrow, we're bringing a spirit medium to perform a ritual and drive them away.

196
15:14.021 --> 15:15.355
Why don't you come with us?

197
15:20.355 --> 15:22.813
Let me go! Where are you taking me?

198
15:22.896 --> 15:25.230
Hey! What's going on?

199
15:25.813 --> 15:28.938
He's possessed again. We're taking him to the spirit medium.

200
15:32.771 --> 15:33.813
What's going on here?

201
15:33.896 --> 15:35.146
I want to go home.

202
15:36.063 --> 15:39.313
They're police officers. They're here to help find Mued.

203
15:39.396 --> 15:40.813
About time you got here, Officer.

204
15:40.896 --> 15:42.563
This ghost's already eaten Mued.

205
15:42.646 --> 15:45.105
Ever since he got possessed, Mued's gone missing.

206
15:45.730 --> 15:46.938
Narong!

207
15:47.021 --> 15:50.855
What did you do to my grandson? Where did you take him?

208
15:54.730 --> 15:55.646
Uncle.

209
15:56.271 --> 15:58.688
I'm Pete, a police officer. I was just transferred here.

210
15:59.230 --> 16:00.896
What happened here?

211
16:01.563 --> 16:02.813
Whose blood is this?

212
16:03.980 --> 16:06.480
He won't answer you, Officer. He's a Phii Pong.

213
16:06.563 --> 16:08.438
Just throw him in jail.

214
16:11.480 --> 16:13.813
You two didn't hurt him, did you?

215
16:14.355 --> 16:18.063
You can't beat him up because you think he's a Phii Pong.

216
16:18.146 --> 16:20.021
It's against the law.

217
16:20.105 --> 16:21.563
It's my blood.

218
16:25.146 --> 16:27.021
I was holding a knife.

219
16:27.105 --> 16:28.521
He came up from behind me

220
16:28.605 --> 16:30.188
and saw that I'd cut myself,

221
16:30.271 --> 16:32.146
so he went to get help.

222
16:34.063 --> 16:36.813
He wasn't helping you. He was running into the forest.

223
16:36.896 --> 16:38.938
He's a Phii Pong and went into the forest to hunt.

224
16:39.021 --> 16:40.688
No one's a ghost.

225
16:43.230 --> 16:45.021
He has a Buddha amulet around his neck.

226
16:46.521 --> 16:48.896
No ghosts can possibly come near him, right?

227
16:53.271 --> 16:54.938
Do you two live together?

228
16:57.313 --> 17:00.521
Let's go to the hospital first. I'll take you.

229
17:01.105 --> 17:03.896
It's all right. The cut isn't deep. It'll heal.

230
17:03.980 --> 17:06.063
I'm not going to do anything.

231
17:06.146 --> 17:08.355
Just come to the hospital with me. I'll drive you.

232
17:08.438 --> 17:09.980
And he can get checked out too.

233
17:46.146 --> 17:47.230
What's going on?

234
17:47.313 --> 17:50.271
It's your father. He's possessed.

235
17:59.938 --> 18:02.188
Go wash your hands. Hospitals are full of germs.

236
18:02.271 --> 18:03.105
Okay.

237
18:08.813 --> 18:10.105
I'm his daughter.

238
18:10.188 --> 18:11.480
Wanrudee Kudprathum.

239
18:12.021 --> 18:13.771
We're treating your mother's wound.

240
18:14.271 --> 18:16.563
-And your father… -Narong Kudprathum.

241
18:17.105 --> 18:20.980
The doctor is assessing his condition. We'll keep you updated.

242
18:23.521 --> 18:24.438
Hello.

243
18:28.813 --> 18:30.438
Are you their daughter?

244
18:31.521 --> 18:32.771
Yes.

245
18:32.855 --> 18:34.855
Miss Wanrudee.

246
18:37.271 --> 18:39.646
Has your father been like this for long?

247
18:43.105 --> 18:44.480
No, never.

248
18:46.188 --> 18:48.146
But you don't live with them, do you?

249
18:48.646 --> 18:50.230
So how would you know that?

250
18:50.313 --> 18:53.730
People in the neighborhood said your father's been like this for a while.

251
18:53.813 --> 18:55.688
I visit them regularly.

252
18:55.771 --> 18:57.563
I don't leave them there alone.

253
18:58.355 --> 19:00.230
He was fine the last time I saw him.

254
19:00.313 --> 19:02.105
How long ago was that?

255
19:02.980 --> 19:05.396
If this is a neurological condition, I'd say it's serious.

256
19:05.480 --> 19:07.938
Shouldn't we wait for the doctor to assess him?

257
19:08.438 --> 19:11.813
A cop shouldn't be able to diagnose a medical condition,

258
19:12.355 --> 19:13.230
right?

259
19:16.771 --> 19:17.896
All right, then.

260
19:17.980 --> 19:21.021
Please give this to your father.

261
19:21.105 --> 19:23.521
I'd like to talk to him when he wakes up

262
19:24.230 --> 19:26.563
and after the doctor has made a diagnosis.

263
19:29.063 --> 19:31.438
POLICE MAJOR SASIDIT DESAYAKUL

264
19:32.271 --> 19:34.605
If my father has done something illegal,

265
19:34.688 --> 19:36.438
you can just tell me.

266
19:36.521 --> 19:37.730
He's done nothing so far.

267
19:37.813 --> 19:39.813
No one's filed any charges against him.

268
19:40.355 --> 19:42.563
I just think your mother's wound looks strange,

269
19:44.105 --> 19:45.563
from a cop's perspective.

270
19:45.646 --> 19:49.521
Let me go! Let go! Why did you bring me here?

271
19:49.605 --> 19:52.396
-Let me go! -Please calm down.

272
19:52.480 --> 19:56.063
I'm not taking any medicine. There's nothing wrong with me!

273
19:56.146 --> 20:01.646
You're ganging up to take my land and give it to her, aren't you?

274
20:01.730 --> 20:06.438
-Let me go! Let go! -Please calm down.

275
20:08.771 --> 20:10.730
Based on my assessment,

276
20:10.813 --> 20:13.521
he's showing signs of dementia.

277
20:15.063 --> 20:20.563
His agitated behavior and his tendency to dwell on the past

278
20:20.646 --> 20:24.896
suggest that those memories are still lingering in his mind.

279
20:25.896 --> 20:26.855
Then…

280
20:28.105 --> 20:29.730
how do we treat it?

281
20:30.313 --> 20:31.605
To be honest with you,

282
20:31.688 --> 20:34.980
dementia can't be cured.

283
20:35.605 --> 20:38.855
The medication I prescribe can only slow its progression

284
20:38.938 --> 20:41.605
so the symptoms don't worsen too quickly.

285
20:42.188 --> 20:44.271
But to be honest, I think

286
20:44.355 --> 20:47.396
your family should start preparing to care for him closely.

287
20:48.688 --> 20:52.896
In the future, he may need round-the-clock care.

288
20:52.980 --> 20:55.188
Let's admit him to the hospital tonight.

289
20:55.271 --> 20:57.813
You can take him home after he wakes up in the morning.

290
20:59.230 --> 21:03.396
EXAMINATION ROOM

291
21:03.480 --> 21:06.730
YOTE

292
21:08.313 --> 21:10.438
-Hello. -Where did you take Aim?

293
21:11.105 --> 21:13.146
I told you he was staying with me tonight.

294
21:13.646 --> 21:15.313
Don't you understand?

295
21:17.063 --> 21:20.646
From now on, you must tell me before you take my son anywhere, got it?

296
21:21.688 --> 21:23.896
Are you listening, bitch?

297
21:23.980 --> 21:25.855
Why aren't you saying anything? Hello?

298
21:26.813 --> 21:27.646
Wan…

299
21:57.938 --> 21:59.855
You have to take your medicine after breakfast.

300
21:59.938 --> 22:01.355
I'll set it aside for you.

301
22:03.771 --> 22:07.271
Mom, I'll clean it up. Go get some rest.

302
22:07.355 --> 22:10.188
You don't clean as well as I do.

303
22:21.896 --> 22:23.313
Did Dad do this to you?

304
22:28.813 --> 22:31.063
I don't know what he thought I was.

305
22:31.896 --> 22:35.646
He came at me with a knife, trying to kill me.

306
22:35.730 --> 22:38.313
I don't know what's gotten into him.

307
22:38.396 --> 22:41.021
Maybe it's a Buddhist holy day.

308
22:41.105 --> 22:44.146
Some spirit must've gotten into him.

309
22:44.771 --> 22:46.355
Where's the knife?

310
22:47.813 --> 22:49.271
I hid it.

311
22:51.021 --> 22:52.855
How long has he been like this?

312
22:59.938 --> 23:00.896
Mom.

313
23:04.188 --> 23:06.521
The doctor said Dad's sick.

314
23:08.771 --> 23:10.563
It has nothing to do with ghosts.

315
23:11.771 --> 23:16.146
What would the doctor know? I live with your father every day.

316
23:16.230 --> 23:19.980
If he wasn't possessed, he wouldn't have hurt me.

317
23:23.188 --> 23:24.396
Go to bed.

318
23:28.230 --> 23:30.521
Why don't you go charge your tablet?

319
23:45.480 --> 23:46.313
Mom.

320
23:46.396 --> 23:48.855
-Yes? -What's wrong with Grandpa?

321
23:49.855 --> 23:51.688
Why was he crying for help?

322
23:53.730 --> 23:55.230
He's sick.

323
23:56.938 --> 23:58.938
But we still don't know what's wrong with him.

324
24:00.688 --> 24:02.813
Can he be treated?

325
24:07.605 --> 24:08.521
Okay.

326
24:09.980 --> 24:10.855
Mom.

327
24:11.938 --> 24:13.605
Do you think

328
24:14.313 --> 24:16.313
there really are Phii Pong around here?

329
24:17.063 --> 24:18.605
No.

330
24:19.355 --> 24:21.063
Where did you get that from?

331
24:23.063 --> 24:25.105
Everyone's talking about them.

332
24:25.813 --> 24:27.105
There aren't any.

333
24:28.313 --> 24:29.980
It's just a story people pass down.

334
24:31.230 --> 24:32.313
Listen to me.

335
24:33.188 --> 24:34.688
Who knows if those telling the story

336
24:35.313 --> 24:36.980
have actually seen one?

337
24:38.188 --> 24:39.771
-Right? -Yes.

338
24:39.855 --> 24:40.688
Right.

339
24:42.271 --> 24:43.105
Come on.

340
24:52.230 --> 24:53.563
-Mom. -Yes?

341
24:53.646 --> 24:55.355
Go brush your teeth.

342
24:55.438 --> 24:57.521
I've already put the toothpaste on for you.

343
25:04.396 --> 25:05.480
What are you looking at?

344
25:06.605 --> 25:08.188
Looks like someone has a mustache.

345
25:09.438 --> 25:10.271
Right?

346
25:12.896 --> 25:14.938
There, I see it.

347
25:15.021 --> 25:17.063
-Wow, it's getting pretty thick. -No, it isn't.

348
25:17.146 --> 25:18.313
-Time to start shaving. -No.

349
25:18.396 --> 25:19.896
Stop! Please, stop!

350
25:19.980 --> 25:22.063
That's enough.

351
25:22.146 --> 25:24.063
That tickles!

352
25:25.605 --> 25:27.230
Aren't you forgetting something?

353
25:27.313 --> 25:28.146
Huh?

354
25:44.813 --> 25:45.980
-Bye-bye. -Sweet dreams, dear.

355
26:04.855 --> 26:08.730
Behold,

356
26:08.813 --> 26:12.730
O gods and celestial beings.

357
26:13.313 --> 26:18.771
You who abide in every tree and mountain-wood,

358
26:18.855 --> 26:22.646
in every deep forest and wilderness,

359
26:22.730 --> 26:27.521
in all rivers, pools, and fish-bays.

360
26:27.605 --> 26:31.813
Gather, all you hosts of deities.

361
27:00.313 --> 27:01.813
Mued.

362
27:01.896 --> 27:05.521
Escape the evil spirits and come back to me.

363
27:21.396 --> 27:22.480
Get out!

364
27:22.563 --> 27:26.146
-Get out! -Get out!

365
27:26.230 --> 27:28.938
-Get out! -Get out!

366
27:29.021 --> 27:35.855
-Get out! -Get out!

367
28:09.105 --> 28:14.105
FAMILY WAITING AREA

368
28:21.938 --> 28:23.813
Do you still like dangerously-sweet treats?

369
28:25.355 --> 28:26.896
Wat, not funny.

370
28:35.688 --> 28:37.855
How long has he been in there?

371
28:38.813 --> 28:40.021
A while.

372
28:42.813 --> 28:45.605
But a CT scan shouldn't take long.

373
28:45.688 --> 28:46.855
He'll be out soon.

374
28:49.646 --> 28:51.355
How's Mom doing?

375
28:54.438 --> 28:56.063
Her wound seems fine.

376
28:58.021 --> 29:00.188
Wat… are you busy?

377
29:01.146 --> 29:02.438
You should go and visit her.

378
29:04.480 --> 29:05.480
Okay.

379
29:06.063 --> 29:07.688
I swapped shifts.

380
29:11.313 --> 29:13.313
If the medication doesn't help Dad,

381
29:14.188 --> 29:17.063
maybe we should move him to a care facility.

382
29:17.855 --> 29:20.063
This illness causes mood swings.

383
29:20.146 --> 29:22.063
We won't be able to manage on our own.

384
29:22.146 --> 29:24.230
Let's try the medication first.

385
29:24.313 --> 29:26.271
I'll just keep going back and forth.

386
29:27.313 --> 29:28.855
I don't want to leave him to others.

387
29:32.188 --> 29:33.313
Can you manage?

388
29:33.396 --> 29:35.188
I'll have to.

389
29:35.855 --> 29:37.980
I've been taking care of him all by myself anyway.

390
29:52.813 --> 29:53.688
Dad.

391
29:55.146 --> 29:58.230
The patient's condition has improved.

392
29:58.313 --> 29:59.896
But don't worry.

393
29:59.980 --> 30:02.813
If his symptoms come back after you take him home,

394
30:02.896 --> 30:05.563
you can call the hospital at any time.

395
30:05.646 --> 30:06.688
Okay.

396
30:40.855 --> 30:42.438
Fill it up yourself.

397
30:44.521 --> 30:47.188
Be especially careful around dusk.

398
30:47.813 --> 30:49.521
Don't go wandering off.

399
30:49.605 --> 30:51.855
Your home is close to the forest and the mountains.

400
30:52.396 --> 30:57.646
If you hear anything at night, don't call it out.

401
30:57.730 --> 31:02.896
Keep your mind steady, and pray before you go to sleep.

402
31:08.105 --> 31:14.771
-Get out! -Get out!

403
31:14.855 --> 31:18.146
-Get out! -Get out!

404
31:36.063 --> 31:37.605
Get out!

405
31:46.021 --> 31:50.688
-Get out! -Get out!

406
31:51.771 --> 31:52.771
Open the gate, kid.

407
31:54.730 --> 31:55.771
Get out!

408
31:55.855 --> 32:02.855
-Get out! -Get out!

409
32:02.938 --> 32:07.480
-Get out! -Get out!

410
32:09.188 --> 32:10.563
Do you live here?

411
32:11.563 --> 32:12.730
Yes.

412
32:12.813 --> 32:15.105
This house is haunted.

413
32:17.480 --> 32:19.521
-No, it isn't. -Your grandpa's a Phii Pong.

414
32:19.605 --> 32:24.188
-Get out! -Get out!

415
32:26.105 --> 32:30.688
-Get out! -Get out!

416
32:30.771 --> 32:33.271
-Get out! -Get out!

417
32:35.688 --> 32:38.438
-Get out! -Get out!

418
32:53.063 --> 32:56.271
Sadhu.

419
32:56.355 --> 33:00.105
Spirits of the land, mountains, forests, and city.

420
33:00.188 --> 33:03.771
If our children who became lost in the forest or the town

421
33:03.855 --> 33:08.980
have unintentionally offended you, by body, mind, or speech,

422
33:09.063 --> 33:15.688
I humbly ask for your forgiveness.

423
33:15.771 --> 33:18.563
Please open the gates,

424
33:18.646 --> 33:22.646
and show them the way,

425
33:22.730 --> 33:25.771
and protect them

426
33:25.855 --> 33:29.938
from harm, danger, or misfortune.

427
33:30.021 --> 33:34.230
Open the way.

428
33:59.396 --> 34:00.938
Let's go.

429
34:58.396 --> 35:01.105
-Hey. -You caught me.

430
35:01.188 --> 35:02.188
Hello, Uncle Wat.

431
35:02.271 --> 35:04.855
Hi, what are you up to?

432
35:05.605 --> 35:08.355
I wanted to see what they were doing.

433
35:08.438 --> 35:09.480
I see.

434
35:10.980 --> 35:13.063
These strange rituals are common around here.

435
35:13.146 --> 35:14.980
You won't find anything like this in the city.

436
35:16.646 --> 35:17.688
Are you scared?

437
35:20.063 --> 35:22.438
The mosquitoes are coming out, want to head inside?

438
35:22.521 --> 35:23.605
-Okay. -Let's go.

439
35:23.688 --> 35:24.813
-Come on. -Okay.

440
36:39.896 --> 36:41.313
Here.

441
36:49.646 --> 36:51.396
Sit down.

442
36:58.563 --> 36:59.396
Here.

443
37:05.813 --> 37:08.480
Yay! I got one. Do you want to play?

444
37:13.063 --> 37:13.980
Come on.

445
37:19.313 --> 37:20.146
Can you do it?

446
37:20.230 --> 37:21.105
Come on.

447
37:21.605 --> 37:22.980
I'll help you.

448
37:29.063 --> 37:30.230
That's it.

449
37:30.855 --> 37:31.688
Hey.

450
37:32.230 --> 37:34.855
Yay, you got it. Very good!

451
38:05.646 --> 38:06.938
What's wrong, Grandpa?

452
38:07.688 --> 38:08.521
Grandpa.

453
38:15.021 --> 38:16.896
Come on, don't cry.

454
38:20.855 --> 38:22.646
Keep playing.

455
39:10.188 --> 39:13.396
What time are you bringing him back? He has taekwondo tomorrow.

456
39:13.480 --> 39:16.396
He'll be there before class.

457
39:16.480 --> 39:17.771
I'll pick him up now

458
39:17.855 --> 39:19.646
so he won't have to wake up early tomorrow.

459
39:19.730 --> 39:22.188
Why would you come here?

460
39:22.271 --> 39:24.355
By the time you get here, he'll probably be asleep.

461
39:27.271 --> 39:29.730
Just go take care of whatever you need to do.

462
39:30.855 --> 39:32.730
Don't worry. I can take care of my son.

463
39:32.813 --> 39:34.063
What did you just say?

464
39:34.146 --> 39:36.896
Wan, what did you just say?

465
42:28.355 --> 42:29.521
Mom.

466
42:29.605 --> 42:31.146
Mom.

467
42:32.438 --> 42:33.480
Mom.

468
45:23.021 --> 45:25.313
Grandpa!

469
45:26.355 --> 45:27.438
Grandpa!

470
45:28.813 --> 45:30.146
Grandpa.

471
52:26.105 --> 52:31.105
Subtitle translation by: Parida Kim
